the big reason why I wrote this book was  because you know society says that the  person who is sitting alone at the  cafeteria is doing so because he or she  is an introvert that likes their  solitude and that may very well be the  case in many different cases however the  person sitting alone could just be  sitting there because they were  extremely shy and have extreme social  anxiety and they could be a really  social person but their brain their  nervous system just doesn't let them and  really what social anxiety is is  essentially what happens is it  essentially strips your nervous system  from having free will and what I mean is  you know social anxiety is not something  random that can happen to you like the  same way that like you can be born an  introvert people are not usually born  with social anxiety what happens is the  onset of it is around nine ten eleven  and usually what happens is you are put  in some sort of a psychologically  traumatizing event that usually involve  social humiliation that essentially  teaches your brain that you should never  speak up again and like personally for  me you know I ended up going to I ended  up living in a small town by the time I  was nine ten eleven that had five  thousand people and then with no racial  diversity and this was also time of post  9/11 in America and my parents had come  from Egypt Middle Eastern and I was  basically placed to this environment  where nobody around me looked like me at  all and then also you get this bullying  abuse people telling me death threats  all the stuff me seen this as a kid that  basically made my brain fall into this  regression of like everyone hates you  nobody likes you and then every  situation every environment that I was  in my brain was just like Mark look to  the ground don't talk to anybody I'd  never speak up  and you know that was my life for about  ten years and that is extremely  different than just being an introvert  and so I like in a lot of different  places whether it was corporations or  schools or wherever would I go speak I  could almost like immediately see who  had social anxiety because I had lived  it like you can see it in their eyes and  I think the final thing that actually  made me write this book  Brian was when I actually began to do  research and look at the data I actually  found out that social anxiety is the  most common form of anxiety in America  and on top of that out of all the other  anxiety conditions social anxiety is the  most correlated with substance abuse as  well as social isolation both social  isolation and substance abuse are linked  to higher rates of suicide and when I  was looking through my life I was like  wait I literally went through social  anxiety substance abuse social isolation  and even suicide and I'm like wow how  many people out of the 850,000 people  that commit suicide every year are doing  so because they have social anxiety and  they can't talk about it with other  people and then you begin to look at  sort of society's mainstream solutions  for kind of addressing mental health  like you know if someone's mental state  really gets that low then they can call  the suicide hotline a doctor a therapist  and and those are all great but the  reality is is that it's hard enough for  the average person to speak about their  mental health issues it is 10,000 times  harder for someone who has social  anxiety to speak on their mental health  issues and I could have you know I could  have easily see myself you know becoming  a statistic but I'm glad I didn't and  I'm glad I was able to write this book  and just kind of show people like hey  here is my own personal story so that  people can use this as a vehicle for  them for their own understanding but  then also I didn't want to I don't want  to write a book that just kind of like  talked about my story and just kind of  anecdotally  people hey here's what you can do I  really wanted to back it up by science  and to show that there are like these  real verifiable credible ways done  through like peer-reviewed clinical  studies that literally show hey this is  what you do if you have social anxiety  here's what works here's what doesn't  work here's what could work here's  what's probably not gonna work for you  and so yeah that was like the major part  of it like once I saw that like once my  brain like completed all these dots I  was like I literally have to write a  book because I personally don't see a  book that kind of talks about this  picture and how to like go about this  and how to manage it in your own life
 

